        "original_id": "876d1087-a535-51ce-8482-f592829d06e9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: 79 Pall Mall, Pall Mall, London\n- People: Nell Gwyn, King Charles II, Zoe Tapper, Richard Eyre\n- Concepts: Grade II listed building, blue plaque\n- Works: Stage Beauty\n\nFacts:\n- Nell Gwyn, also spelled Gwynn or Gwynne, was born on 2 February 1650 and died on 14 November 1687.\n- Nell Gwyn was a long-time mistress of King Charles II of England and Scotland.\n- After retiring from the stage, Nell Gwyn occupied a brick townhouse on the site of what is now 79 Pall Mall, and a blue plaque marks this.\n- 79 Pall Mall is a Grade II listed building on Pall Mall in London.\n- Zoe Tapper was born on 26 October 1981 and is an English actress.\n- In 2004, Zoe Tapper first came to prominence by playing Nell Gwynne in Richard Eyre's award-winning film Stage Beauty.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
